; Element order is semantic (design 2026-07-17). The convention-ordered
; incenter rabbit ear (--ea .a)(--ec .c) leading — whose <180 arc is the big
; stayer sector — folds cleanly (flatten-rabbit-ear-toward-a.bel). Reorder the
; SAME three creases so the leading pair is (--eb .b)(--ea .a): now the
; conventional arc is a small folding sector, the ear is anchored on material
; that must move, and no seating keeps the flap in the sheet. Reordering the
; items — nothing else — flips a valid fold into an error.

paper square

mark --diag = through .a .c
mark --ea = map --ab onto --diag
mark --eb = map --ab onto --bc
mark --ec = map --bc onto --diag

flatten (--eb & .b) (--ea & .a) (--ec & .c) {toward .a}

; expect error "off the paper"
